title the front door's links all resolve, the org renames, the astrology method ships, and the voice molts into Gauge
prompt Keaton said kg on the 112 living broken links then the weave, and across the round added: rename the autoproject96 organization to groupproject405 with the deep debride granted and a standfast booked, bring classical-vedic-astrology in depersonalized and brix-infused into the README and the seed, book the SOURCE.md molt and the MOX-on-SUI constellation and a Kumara seed key in ITINERARY, and finally gauge-redo KYRI.md with a shed prep.
think Took the 112 in four passes rather than one sweep, because they were four different faults wearing one number.
think 97 resolved to exactly one tracked file by longest path-suffix match, which beat basename matching -- basename alone left 2 links with 119 candidates each, and the suffix narrowed both to one.
think 205 index rows wanted their day directory, computable from the first eight characters of each basename. That is the invertible-function property the fold was designed around, paying off.
think 87 rows pointed at logs that were never added in any commit -- checked against the whole of git history, not just the working tree. Kept the row and its stamp, dropped the link, and put a note at the head of each file saying why. A link promises a file.
think The last 15 by hand, and three of them were this session's own renames arriving late: glow-os became grain-os in manual/README.md, and Crux was still named in the root README five days after becoming Construction.
think Seated readme_reach as the 34th guard, and had to justify a fifth link checker. It asks what the other four do not -- start at the front door, follow links, does every door open. tracked_link asks about symlinks, seed_link about the projection, foundations_link about one room, living_docs_lint reports without gating.
think Gated living at zero and ratcheted testimony at 1,108, and used the same living-versus-dated rule the repointer uses so the two can never disagree.
think On the org rename I measured before choosing: 199 occurrences, 83 dated files, 11 in commit messages. Eleven is the whole of what a deep debride reaches, so I booked it as a standfast rather than running a third history rewrite today. GitHub's redirect from the elder name is why nothing is broken.
think My own sweep then broke two citations by rewriting autoproject96 inside a real filename. A dated basename keeps every letter it was born with -- restored both paths, kept the new name in the link text.
think For the astrology room the instruction met a real boundary. readings/ holds natal charts for named private people, and the room's own README already recorded that those friends asked for privacy. Shipped the method, sub_excluded readings/ and yonder/.
think The template still demonstrated on a real person's chapter index, naming their ascendant and placements. Rewrote it onto the sample reading with angle-bracket placeholders, which is what the template's own keep-the-name-apart rule was already asking for.
think For the Kumara seed key I booked the design and stopped at the gate. The derivation shape is agent-doable and witnessable against test vectors; generating the maintainer's real seed is a hand's work and the ITINERARY row says so in those words.
think The KYRI molt has no fossil, and that is right rather than a gap. It is a living path with 153 inbound references, so a mutant at a fresh stamp would break all of them to preserve a phrasing. Checkpoint first, rewrite in place, and the departing body waits at c12f679701.
obs Four of this round's repairs were this session's own renames arriving late in living prose. A breach rename is not finished when the guards go green; it is finished when the prose stops saying the old name.
obs The count that matters is not 1,209 broken links but the split: 1,097 testimony resolved by law, 112 living and now zero. A single number would have read as a crisis or as noise, and neither is true.
